  abstract      = {We study the shape, alignment, and mass distribution of baryonic and dark-matter halos in the EAGLE cosmological hydrodynamic simulation using an iterative principal component analysis. Dark-matter halos are triaxial, with median axis ratios b/a and c/a of about 0.82 and 0.64. Baryons make the inner halo rounder and align the stellar and dark-matter components, while the outer halo retains its triaxial shape.},
